IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `s121-nouns`
IMPORT `s121-support`

-- 26 U.S.C. section 121. LAYER 1, module 4: subsection (d)(9) to (d)(12): service abroad or away, like-kind property, and the Peace Corps.
-- Placed before the other subsections because (b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) uses its definition of "qualified official extended duty".
-- Borrowed terms are inputs: "uniformed services" (title 10 section 101(a)(5)), "member of the Service" (Foreign Service Act section 103),
-- "employee" (title 5 section 2105), the Peace Corps Act sections 5 and 6, and section 1031 are not among the sources.
-- Time: the 5-year period "suspended" by an election is computed by walking back from the sale date, counting only days not suspended (fork F7).

§ `Subsection (d)(9): uniformed services, Foreign Service, and intelligence community`

-- src:134 | (v) Extended duty
-- src:135 | The term “extended duty” means any period of active duty pursuant to a call or order to such duty for a period in excess of 90 days or for an indefinite period.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(v) (src:134-135)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(v) the duty is extended duty` MEANS
    IF service's `on active duty pursuant to a call or order`
         AND (   service's `days the call or order is for` GREATER THAN 90
              OR service's `the call or order is for an indefinite period`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “extended duty” means any period of active duty pursuant to a call or order to such duty for a period in excess of 90 days or for an indefinite period."
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- src:116 | (i) In general
-- src:117 | The term “qualified official extended duty” means any extended duty while serving at a duty station which is at least 50 miles from such property or while residing under Government orders in Government quarters.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) (src:116-117)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) the duty is qualified official extended duty` MEANS
    IF    service's `miles from the duty station to the property` AT LEAST 50
       OR service's `residing under Government orders in Government quarters`
    THEN `s 121(d)(9)(C)(v) the duty is extended duty` service
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “qualified official extended duty” means any extended duty while serving at a duty station which is at least 50 miles from such property or while residing under Government orders in Government quarters."
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (ii) and (iii): the meanings are given by title 10 and the Foreign Service Act, which are not among the sources. The caller states the borrowed fact.
-- src:118 | (ii) Uniformed services
-- src:119 | The term “uniformed services” has the meaning given such term by section 101(a)(5) of title 10, United States Code, as in effect on the date of the enactment of this paragraph.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(ii) (src:118-119)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(ii) the person is a member of the uniformed services` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given such term by section 101(a)(5) of title 10, United States Code" -- the caller's answer is read as the meaning.
    JUST (service's `a member of the uniformed services under section 101(a)(5) of title 10`)

-- src:120 | (iii) Foreign Service of the United States
-- src:121 | The term “member of the Foreign Service of the United States” has the meaning given the term “member of the Service” by paragraph (1), (2), (3), (4), or (5) of section 103 of the Foreign Service Act of 1980, as in effect on the date of the enactment of this paragraph.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(iii) (src:120-121)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iii) the person is a member of the Foreign Service of the United States` MEANS
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given the term “member of the Service” by paragraph (1), (2), (3), (4), or (5) of section 103 of the Foreign Service Act of 1980" -- the caller's answer is read as the meaning.
    JUST (service's `a member of the Service under section 103(1) to (5) of the Foreign Service Act of 1980`)

-- (iv): the ten clauses (I) to (X); clause (VIII) lists eight elements. The label of the clause that names an office:
-- src:122 | (iv) Employee of intelligence community
-- src:123 | The term “employee of the intelligence community” means an employee (as defined by section 2105 of title 5, United States Code) of—
-- src:124 | (I) the Office of the Director of National Intelligence,
-- src:125 | (II) the Central Intelligence Agency,
-- src:126 | (III) the National Security Agency,
-- src:127 | (IV) the Defense Intelligence Agency,
-- src:128 | (V) the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency,
-- src:129 | (VI) the National Reconnaissance Office,
-- src:130 | (VII) any other office within the Department of Defense for the collection of specialized national intelligence through reconnaissance programs,
-- src:131 | (VIII) any of the intelligence elements of the Army, the Navy, the Air Force, the Marine Corps, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, the Department of Treasury, the Department of Energy, and the Coast Guard,
-- src:132 | (IX) the Bureau of Intelligence and Research of the Department of State, or
-- src:133 | (X) any of the elements of the Department of Homeland Security concerned with the analyses of foreign intelligence information.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) (src:122-133)
GIVEN office IS AN `Office of the intelligence community`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) the clause that names the office` MEANS
    CONSIDER office
    WHEN `the Office of the Director of National Intelligence` THEN JUST "(I)"
    WHEN `the Central Intelligence Agency` THEN JUST "(II)"
    WHEN `the National Security Agency` THEN JUST "(III)"
    WHEN `the Defense Intelligence Agency` THEN JUST "(IV)"
    WHEN `the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency` THEN JUST "(V)"
    WHEN `the National Reconnaissance Office` THEN JUST "(VI)"
    WHEN `another office within the Department of Defense for the collection of specialized national intelligence through reconnaissance programs` THEN JUST "(VII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Army` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Navy` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Air Force` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Marine Corps` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Federal Bureau of Investigation` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Department of Treasury` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Department of Energy` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `an intelligence element of the Coast Guard` THEN JUST "(VIII)"
    WHEN `the Bureau of Intelligence and Research of the Department of State` THEN JUST "(IX)"
    WHEN `an element of the Department of Homeland Security concerned with the analyses of foreign intelligence information` THEN JUST "(X)"
    -- NOTHING-kind (silent): an office the text does not name has no clause.
    WHEN `some other office` THEN NOTHING

-- src:122 | (iv) Employee of intelligence community
-- src:123 | The term “employee of the intelligence community” means an employee (as defined by section 2105 of title 5, United States Code) of—
-- src:124 | (I) the Office of the Director of National Intelligence,
-- src:125 | (II) the Central Intelligence Agency,
-- src:126 | (III) the National Security Agency,
-- src:127 | (IV) the Defense Intelligence Agency,
-- src:128 | (V) the National Geospatial-Intelligence Agency,
-- src:129 | (VI) the National Reconnaissance Office,
-- src:130 | (VII) any other office within the Department of Defense for the collection of specialized national intelligence through reconnaissance programs,
-- src:131 | (VIII) any of the intelligence elements of the Army, the Navy, the Air Force, the Marine Corps, the Federal Bureau of Investigation, the Department of Treasury, the Department of Energy, and the Coast Guard,
-- src:132 | (IX) the Bureau of Intelligence and Research of the Department of State, or
-- src:133 | (X) any of the elements of the Department of Homeland Security concerned with the analyses of foreign intelligence information.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) (src:122-133)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) the person is an employee of the intelligence community` MEANS
    IF service's `an employee as defined by section 2105 of title 5`
         AND NOT (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) the clause that names the office` (service's `office of the intelligence community`) EQUALS NOTHING)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The term “employee of the intelligence community” means an employee (as defined by section 2105 of title 5, United States Code) of— (I) ... (X) ..." (a "means" definition: not an employee, or an office the list does not name)
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- (A): the three capacities in which duty counts, and (C)(i)'s qualified official extended duty.
-- src:107 | (A) In general
-- src:108 | At the election of an individual with respect to a property, the running of the 5-year period described in subsections (a) and (c)(1)(B) and paragraph (7) of this subsection with respect to such property shall be suspended during any period that such individual or such individual’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty—
-- src:109 | (i) as a member of the uniformed services,
-- src:110 | (ii) as a member of the Foreign Service of the United States, or
-- src:111 | (iii) as an employee of the intelligence community.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(A) (src:107-111)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(A) the service is qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii)` MEANS
    CONSIDER service's `capacity`
    WHEN `member of the uniformed services` THEN
        `both are true` (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(ii) the person is a member of the uniformed services` service) (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) the duty is qualified official extended duty` service)
    WHEN `member of the Foreign Service of the United States` THEN
        `both are true` (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iii) the person is a member of the Foreign Service of the United States` service) (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) the duty is qualified official extended duty` service)
    WHEN `employee of the intelligence community` THEN
        `both are true` (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(iv) the person is an employee of the intelligence community` service) (`s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) the duty is qualified official extended duty` service)
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the suspension is granted for service "(i) as a member of the uniformed services, (ii) as a member of the Foreign Service of the United States, or (iii) as an employee of the intelligence community"; other service is outside the limit.
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (D): the election. "An election ... may not be made if such an election is in effect with respect to any other property."
-- src:136 | (D) Special rules relating to election
-- src:137 | (i) Election limited to 1 property at a time
-- src:138 | An election under subparagraph (A) with respect to any property may not be made if such an election is in effect with respect to any other property.
-- src:139 | (ii) Revocation of election
-- src:140 | An election under subparagraph (A) may be revoked at any time.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(D) (src:136-140)
GIVEN `the individual elects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election under subparagraph (A) is in effect for another property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(9)(A) the running of the 5-year period is suspended at the individual's election` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the individual elects`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the suspension is "At the election of an individual"; with no election the text is silent.
            NOTHING
        IF `an election under subparagraph (A) is in effect for another property` THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An election under subparagraph (A) with respect to any property may not be made if such an election is in effect with respect to any other property."
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the election has been revoked` THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "An election under subparagraph (A) may be revoked at any time." does not say in terms what a revoked election does.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- (B): the extension is capped at 10 years. The 5-year period, running back from the sale date, is suspended during qualifying service:
-- walk back from the sale date counting only days that are not suspended until 5 years' worth of days is reached; never go back further than 15 years.
-- `cursor` is the day number of the latest day not yet counted; `budget` is the number of days still to count.
GIVEN cursor IS A NUMBER
      budget IS A NUMBER
      duty IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the day number of the first day, walking back past duty` MEANS
    CONSIDER duty
    WHEN EMPTY THEN cursor MINUS budget PLUS 1
    WHEN s FOLLOWED BY rest THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `the day number of` (s's `last day`) AT LEAST cursor
               THEN `the day number of the first day, walking back past duty` (`the day number of` (s's `first day`) MINUS 1) budget rest
            IF budget AT MOST (cursor MINUS `the day number of` (s's `last day`))
               THEN cursor MINUS budget PLUS 1
            OTHERWISE
               `the day number of the first day, walking back past duty` (`the day number of` (s's `first day`) MINUS 1) (budget MINUS (cursor MINUS `the day number of` (s's `last day`))) rest

-- src:112 | (B) Maximum period of suspension
-- src:113 | The 5-year period described in subsection (a) shall not be extended more than 10 years by reason of subparagraph (A).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(B) (src:112-113)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      `the days of qualifying service` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A Span
`s 121(d)(9)(B) the 5-year period as extended, by no more than 10 years` MEANS
    Span OF (`the date with day number` (`the larger of` walkedBack earliestAllowed)), sale
    WHERE
        fiveYears MEANS `the days in the years ending on` sale 5
        duty MEANS `the spans latest first` (map (GIVEN s YIELD `the overlap of the spans` s (Span OF (Date 1 1 1900), sale)) (`the spans with no day counted twice` `the days of qualifying service`))
        walkedBack MEANS `the day number of the first day, walking back past duty` (`the day number of` sale) fiveYears duty
        earliestAllowed MEANS `the day number of` ((`the span of the years ending on` sale 15)'s `first day`)

-- Whether a period of service suspends the 5-year period: (d)(9)(A)(i)-(iii) or (d)(12)(A) (below).

§ `Subsection (d)(10): property acquired in like-kind exchange`

-- src:141 | (10) Property acquired in like-kind exchange
-- src:142 | If a taxpayer acquires property in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized (in whole or in part) to the taxpayer under subsection (a) or (b) of section 1031, subsection (a) shall not apply to the sale or exchange of such property by such taxpayer (or by any person whose basis in such property is determined, in whole or in part, by reference to the basis in the hands of such taxpayer) during the 5-year period beginning with the date of such acquisition.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(10) (src:141-142)
GIVEN `acquired in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized under subsection (a) or (b) of section 1031` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is the taxpayer or a person whose basis is determined by reference to the taxpayer's basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      acquisition IS A DATE
      sale IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(10) subsection (a) shall not apply to the sale of property acquired in a like-kind exchange` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`acquired in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized under subsection (a) or (b) of section 1031`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If a taxpayer acquires property in an exchange with respect to which gain is not recognized (in whole or in part) to the taxpayer under subsection (a) or (b) of section 1031" (section 1031 is outside the sources)
            NOTHING
        IF NOT (`the seller is the taxpayer or a person whose basis is determined by reference to the taxpayer's basis`) THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by such taxpayer (or by any person whose basis in such property is determined, in whole or in part, by reference to the basis in the hands of such taxpayer)"
            NOTHING
        IF `the date is in the span` sale (`the span of the years beginning with` acquisition 5) THEN JUST TRUE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "during the 5-year period beginning with the date of such acquisition" (a period the text fixes; outside it the bar does not speak)
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

§ `Subsection (d)(11): repealed`

-- The text shows the paragraph repealed; nothing is encoded. The quotation is the whole of what the text holds for (d)(11).
-- src:143 | [(11) Repealed. Pub. L. 111–312, title III, § 301(a), Dec. 17, 2010, 124 Stat. 3300]

§ `Subsection (d)(12): Peace Corps`

-- src:144 | (12) Peace Corps
-- src:145 | (A) In general
-- src:146 | At the election of an individual with respect to a property, the running of the 5-year period described in subsections (a) and (c)(1)(B) and paragraph (7) of this subsection with respect to such property shall be suspended during any period that such individual or such individual’s spouse is serving outside the United States—
-- src:147 | (i) on qualified official extended duty (as defined in paragraph (9)(C)) as an employee of the Peace Corps, or
-- src:148 | (ii) as an enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under section 5 or 6 (as the case may be) of the Peace Corps Act (22 U.S.C. 2504, 2505).
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(12)(A) (src:144-148)
GIVEN service IS A `Period of service`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(12)(A) the service is serving outside the United States as described in clause (i) or (ii)` MEANS
    CONSIDER service's `capacity`
    WHEN `employee of the Peace Corps` THEN
        IF service's `serving outside the United States`
        THEN `s 121(d)(9)(C)(i) the duty is qualified official extended duty` service
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is serving outside the United States— (i) on qualified official extended duty (as defined in paragraph (9)(C)) as an employee of the Peace Corps" (a failed condition of the provision; marginal reading (a))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    WHEN `enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under the Peace Corps Act` THEN
        IF service's `serving outside the United States`
        THEN JUST (   service's `an enrolled volunteer under section 5 of the Peace Corps Act`
                   OR service's `a volunteer leader under section 6 of the Peace Corps Act`)
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is serving outside the United States— ... (ii) as an enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader under section 5 or 6 (as the case may be) of the Peace Corps Act" (a failed condition of the provision; marginal reading (a))
        ELSE JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the suspension is granted for service "(i) on qualified official extended duty ... as an employee of the Peace Corps, or (ii) as an enrolled volunteer or volunteer leader"; other service is outside the limit.
    OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- (B): "rules similar to the rules of subparagraphs (B) and (D) of paragraph (9) shall apply": the same 10-year cap on the extension
-- and the same election rules (one election for one property at a time; revocable). Read here as the same functions (fork F8).
-- src:149 | (B) Applicable rules
-- src:150 | For purposes of subparagraph (A), rules similar to the rules of subparagraphs (B) and (D) of paragraph (9) shall apply.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(12)(B) (src:149-150)
GIVEN sale IS A DATE
      `the days of qualifying service` IS A LIST OF Span
GIVETH A Span
`s 121(d)(12)(B) the 5-year period as extended by rules similar to (d)(9)(B)` MEANS
    `s 121(d)(9)(B) the 5-year period as extended, by no more than 10 years` sale `the days of qualifying service`

-- src:149 | (B) Applicable rules
-- src:150 | For purposes of subparagraph (A), rules similar to the rules of subparagraphs (B) and (D) of paragraph (9) shall apply.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(12)(B) (src:149-150)
GIVEN `the individual elects` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election under subparagraph (A) is in effect for another property` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the election has been revoked` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 121(d)(12)(A) the running of the 5-year period is suspended at the individual's election` MEANS
    `s 121(d)(9)(A) the running of the 5-year period is suspended at the individual's election` `the individual elects` `an election under subparagraph (A) is in effect for another property` `the election has been revoked`

-- Whether a period of service suspends the 5-year period under (d)(9)(A) or (d)(12)(A), as a plain list of the days that do.
-- src:107 | (A) In general
-- src:108 | At the election of an individual with respect to a property, the running of the 5-year period described in subsections (a) and (c)(1)(B) and paragraph (7) of this subsection with respect to such property shall be suspended during any period that such individual or such individual’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty—
-- src:109 | (i) as a member of the uniformed services,
-- src:110 | (ii) as a member of the Foreign Service of the United States, or
-- src:111 | (iii) as an employee of the intelligence community.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(A) and (d)(12)(A) (src:107-111)
GIVEN services IS A LIST OF `Period of service`
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`s 121(d)(9)(A) and (d)(12)(A) the days of service that suspend the 5-year period` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `days`) (filter `the service qualifies` services)
    WHERE
        `the service qualifies` s MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 121(d)(9)(A) the service is qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii)` s
            WHEN JUST yes THEN yes
            WHEN NOTHING THEN
                CONSIDER `s 121(d)(12)(A) the service is serving outside the United States as described in clause (i) or (ii)` s
                WHEN JUST yes THEN yes
                WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

-- The days of qualifying service of (d)(9)(A)(i)-(iii) alone, which is what (b)(5)(C)(ii)(II) names ("described in clause (i), (ii), or (iii) of subsection (d)(9)(A)").
-- src:107 | (A) In general
-- src:108 | At the election of an individual with respect to a property, the running of the 5-year period described in subsections (a) and (c)(1)(B) and paragraph (7) of this subsection with respect to such property shall be suspended during any period that such individual or such individual’s spouse is serving on qualified official extended duty—
-- src:109 | (i) as a member of the uniformed services,
-- src:110 | (ii) as a member of the Foreign Service of the United States, or
-- src:111 | (iii) as an employee of the intelligence community.
@ref 26 U.S.C. s 121(d)(9)(A) (src:107-111)
GIVEN services IS A LIST OF `Period of service`
GIVETH A LIST OF Span
`s 121(d)(9)(A) the days of service on qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii)` MEANS
    map (GIVEN s YIELD s's `days`)
        (filter (GIVEN s YIELD `s 121(d)(9)(A) the service is qualified official extended duty described in clause (i), (ii) or (iii)` s EQUALS JUST TRUE) services)
